    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Reliable data transfer protocol over a channel with bit errors and packet losses is( ) \n\nOptions: \nA. rdt1.0\nB. rdt2.0\nC. rdt3.0\nD. rdt2.1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The rdt3.0 protocol is designed to handle both bit errors and packet losses, incorporating acknowledgments, timeouts, and sequence numbers for reliability. Earlier versions like rdt2.0 and rdt2.1 handle bit errors but assume no packet loss, while rdt1.0 assumes a completely reliable channel. Therefore, rdt3.0 is the most suitable for channels with both bit errors and packet losses.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
