    "global index": "ArcMMLU_335",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose the frequency of the most frequent word in a corpus of Tamil documents is 10000.Whatwould be the estimated frequency of second most frequent in the given corpus as per Zipf's law? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. 10000\nB. 2500\nC. 5000\nD. Cannot be determined\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "According to Zipf's law, the frequency of a word is inversely proportional to its rank in the frequency table. So, if the most frequent word has a frequency of 10000 (rank 1), the second most frequent word (rank 2) would have a frequency of approximately 10000 / 2 = 5000. Therefore, the estimated frequency is 5000.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
