    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximumTime(s: str) -> str:\n    # Convert string to list for easier modification\n    time_list = list(s)\n    \n    # Handle hour part (positions 0 and 1)\n    if time_list[0] == '?' and time_list[1] == '?':\n        # Maximum hour is 11\n        time_list[0] = '1'\n        time_list[1] = '1'\n    elif time_list[0] == '?':\n        # Determine first digit of hour based on second digit\n        if time_list[1] <= '1':\n            time_list[0] = '1'\n        else:\n            time_list[0] = '0'\n    elif time_list[1] == '?':\n        # Determine second digit of hour based on first digit\n        if time_list[0] == '0':\n            time_list[1] = '9'\n        else:  # time_list[0] == '1'\n            time_list[1] = '1'\n    \n    # Handle minute part (positions 3 and 4)\n    if time_list[3] == '?' and time_list[4] == '?':\n        # Maximum minute is 59\n        time_list[3] = '5'\n        time_list[4] = '9'\n    elif time_list[3] == '?':\n        time_list[3] = '5'\n    elif time_list[4] == '?':\n        time_list[4] = '9'\n    \n    return ''.join(time_list)\n```",
