    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minExtraChar(s, dictionary):\n    n = len(s)\n    # dp[i] represents the minimum number of extra characters from index i to the end\n    dp = [float('inf')] * (n + 1)\n    dp[n] = 0  # Base case: no characters left means 0 extra characters\n    \n    # Convert dictionary to a set for O(1) lookups\n    word_set = set(dictionary)\n    \n    # Fill dp array from right to left\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        # Option 1: Consider s[i] as an extra character\n        dp[i] = dp[i + 1] + 1\n        \n        # Option 2: Try to match a word starting at index i\n        for j in range(i + 1, n + 1):\n            if s[i:j] in word_set:\n                dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[j])\n    \n    return dp[0]\n```",
