    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef max_distance(moves: str) -> int:\n    # Count fixed moves and wildcards\n    left_fixed = moves.count('L')\n    right_fixed = moves.count('R')\n    wildcards = moves.count('_')\n    \n    # To maximize distance from origin, we want to maximize absolute value of final position\n    # We have two options:\n    # 1. Go as far right as possible: all wildcards go right\n    # 2. Go as far left as possible: all wildcards go left\n    \n    # Position if all wildcards go right\n    pos_right = right_fixed + wildcards - left_fixed\n    \n    # Position if all wildcards go left\n    pos_left = right_fixed - (left_fixed + wildcards)\n    \n    # Return the maximum absolute value\n    return max(abs(pos_right), abs(pos_left))\n```",
