      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_champion(grid):\n    n = len(grid)\n    # A champion must have 1s in all columns except possibly its own diagonal\n    # Since grid[i][j] == 1 means i is stronger than j, a champion team i \n    # should have grid[i][j] == 1 for all j != i\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        # Check if team i is stronger than all other teams\n        is_champion = True\n        for j in range(n):\n            if i != j and grid[i][j] != 1:\n                is_champion = False\n                break\n        if is_champion:\n            return i\n    \n    # The problem guarantees a unique champion exists, so this line should never be reached\n    return -1\n```",
