    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef shortestSubstrings(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    answer = [\"\"] * n\n    \n    # Precompute all substrings for each string\n    substrings = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        s = arr[i]\n        substr_set = set()\n        for length in range(1, len(s) + 1):\n            for start in range(len(s) - length + 1):\n                substr = s[start:start + length]\n                substr_set.add(substr)\n        substrings.append(substr_set)\n    \n    # For each string, find the shortest lexicographically smallest substring not present in others\n    for i in range(n):\n        best = \"\"\n        s = arr[i]\n        # Try all lengths from 1 to len(s)\n        for length in range(1, len(s) + 1):\n            candidates = []\n            # Generate all substrings of this length from arr[i]\n            for start in range(len(s) - length + 1):\n                substr = s[start:start + length]\n                # Check if this substring appears in any other string\n                found_in_other = False\n                for j in range(n):\n                    if i == j:\n                        continue\n                    if substr in substrings[j]:\n                        found_in_other = True\n                        break\n                \n                if not found_in_other:\n                    candidates.append(substr)\n            \n            # If we found candidates of this length, sort lexicographically and pick the first\n            if candidates:\n                candidates.sort()\n                best = candidates[0]\n                break  # Since we're looking for shortest, we can break after finding candidates\n        \n        answer[i] = best\n    \n    return answer\n```",
