0, 1, and 2. Among these, the answer is the string at index 2 because it has the shortest length of 6.\nFor wordsQuery[1] = \"acbfgh\", only the string at index 0 shares the longest common suffix \"fgh\". Hence it is the answer, even though the string at index 2 is shorter.\nFor wordsQuery[2] = \"acbfegh\", strings from wordsContainer that share the longest common suffix \"gh\" are at indices 0, 1, and 2. Among these, the answer is the string at index 2 because it has the shortest length of 6.\n\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= wordsContainer.length, wordsQuery.length <= 10^4\n1 <= wordsContainer[i].length <= 5 * 10^3\n1 <= wordsQuery[i].length <= 5 * 10^3\nwordsContainer[i] consists only of lowercase English letters.\nwordsQuery[i] consists only of lowercase English letters.\nSum of wordsContainer[i].length is at most 5 * 10^5.\nSum of wordsQuery[i].length is at most 5 * 10^5.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef substring_matching(wordsContainer, wordsQuery):\n    # Build a trie of reversed words from wordsContainer\n    # Each node stores: best_index (index of best word ending at or passing through this node)\n    # A word is better if it's shorter, or same length but appeared earlier\n    \n    # Create the trie node structure\n    # Each node is a dict with keys: 'next' (dict of children), 'best_idx' (int)\n    trie = {'next': {}, 'best_idx': 0}\n    \n    # Preprocess wordsContainer: reverse each word and insert into trie\n    for idx, word in enumerate(wordsContainer):\n        # Update the best candidate if needed at root (for empty suffix)\n        current_best_idx = trie['best_idx']\n        current_word = wordsContainer[current_best_idx]\n        if (len(word) < len(current_word) or \n            (len(word) == len(current_word) and idx < current_best_idx)):\n            trie['best_idx'] = idx\n        \n        # Reverse the word for suffix matching\n        rev_word = word[::-1]\n        node = trie\n        \n        # Traverse the trie\n        for char in rev_word:\n            if char not in node['next']:\n                node['next'][char] = {'next': {}, 'best_idx': idx}\n                node = node['next'][char]\n            else:\n                node = node['next'][char]\n                # Update best index at this node if current word is better\n                current_best_idx = node['best_idx']\n                current_word = wordsContainer[current_best_idx]\n                if (len(word) < len(current_word) or \n                    (len(word) == len(current_word) and idx < current_best_idx)):\n                    node['best_idx'] = idx\n    \n    # Process each query\n    ans = []\n    for query in wordsQuery:\n        # Reverse the query to match suffix in trie (prefix in reversed trie)\n        rev_query = query[::-1]\n        node = trie\n        best_idx = trie['best_idx']  # default to best for empty suffix\n        \n        # Try to follow the trie with reversed query\n        for char in rev_query:\n            if char in node['next']:\n                node = node['next'][char]\n                best_idx = node['best_idx']  # update best for current prefix length\n            else:\n                break  # stop when we can't go further\n        \n        ans.append(best_idx)\n    \n    return ans\n```",
