      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef min_changes(s: str) -> int:\n    # Since each substring in the partition must have even length and be uniform (all 0s or all 1s),\n    # the simplest valid partition is into substrings of length 2 (since the total length is even).\n    # For any valid partition, we can always refine it to only use length-2 substrings without increasing cost.\n    # For each pair of characters (s[2*i], s[2*i+1]), we want them to be the same (so they can form a uniform substring of length 2).\n    # The minimum changes for each pair is:\n    #   - 0 if both characters are already the same\n    #   - 1 if they are different (change one to match the other)\n    changes = 0\n    for i in range(0, len(s), 2):\n        if s[i] != s[i+1]:\n            changes += 1\n    return changes\n```",
