    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longest_semi_repetitive_substring(s: str) -> int:\n    if len(s) <= 1:\n        return len(s)\n    \n    max_len = 1\n    left = 0\n    # Track the last index where we had a consecutive pair\n    last_pair_index = -1\n    \n    for right in range(1, len(s)):\n        # Check if current and previous characters form a consecutive pair\n        if s[right] == s[right - 1]:\n            # If we already have a pair in our current window\n            if last_pair_index != -1:\n                # Move left pointer to after the previous pair's first character\n                left = last_pair_index + 1\n            \n            # Update the last pair index to the current pair's first index\n            last_pair_index = right - 1\n        \n        # Update maximum length\n        max_len = max(max_len, right - left + 1)\n    \n    return max_len\n```",
