    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef minimumDeletions(word: str, k: int) -> int:\n    # Count frequency of each character\n    freq = list(Counter(word).values())\n    n = len(freq)\n    \n    # Sort frequencies in ascending order\n    freq.sort()\n    \n    # Try all possible target frequency ranges [min_freq, min_freq + k]\n    # We'll consider each frequency as a potential minimum in the final multiset\n    min_deletions = float('inf')\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        # Consider making all frequencies fall within [freq[i], freq[i] + k]\n        min_freq = freq[i]\n        max_freq = min_freq + k\n        \n        deletions = 0\n        for j in range(n):\n            if freq[j] < min_freq:\n                # We need to delete all occurrences of this character\n                deletions += freq[j]\n            elif freq[j] > max_freq:\n                # We need to delete (freq[j] - max_freq) occurrences\n                deletions += freq[j] - max_freq\n            # If min_freq <= freq[j] <= max_freq, no deletion needed for this character\n        \n        min_deletions = min(min_deletions, deletions)\n    \n    return min_deletions\n```",
