      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef min_steps_to_group_black_balls(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the minimum number of adjacent swaps needed to group all black balls (1s) to the right\n    and all white balls (0s) to the left.\n    \n    The approach is to count how many white balls (0s) each black ball (1) needs to \"jump over\"\n    to reach its correct position. When we encounter a black ball (1), we count how many white balls\n    (0s) have been encountered so far - this represents the number of swaps needed to move this\n    black ball past all those white balls to its correct position on the right side.\n    \n    Args:\n        s: A binary string where '1' represents black balls and '0' represents white balls\n        \n    Returns:\n        The minimum number of adjacent swaps needed\n    \"\"\"\n    white_count = 0  # Count of white balls (0s) encountered so far\n    swaps = 0  # Total swaps needed\n    \n    for char in s:\n        if char == '0':\n            # This is a white ball, increment the count of white balls seen\n            white_count += 1\n        else:\n            # This is a black ball, it needs to move past all white balls seen so far\n            swaps += white_count\n    \n    return swaps\n```",
