    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef shortest_common_superstring(a, b, c):\n    from itertools import permutations\n    \n    # Function to find the shortest string that contains s1 and s2 as substrings\n    def merge(s1, s2):\n        # If s1 already contains s2, return s1\n        if s2 in s1:\n            return s1\n        # Try all possible overlaps\n        for i in range(min(len(s1), len(s2)), 0, -1):\n            if s1.endswith(s2[:i]):\n                return s1 + s2[i:]\n        return s1 + s2\n    \n    # Check if a string contains all three strings as substrings\n    def contains_all(s, a, b, c):\n        return a in s and b in s and c in s\n    \n    # Try all permutations of the strings\n    best = None\n    for p in permutations([a, b, c]):\n        # Merge first two strings\n        merged = merge(p[0], p[1])\n        # Merge with the third string\n        candidate = merge(merged, p[2])\n        # Check if this candidate contains all strings (to handle cases where merge doesn't guarantee containment)\n        # Actually, our merge function should guarantee this, but let's verify\n        if not contains_all(candidate, a, b, c):\n            continue\n        \n        # Update best candidate\n        if best is None or len(candidate) < len(best) or (len(candidate) == len(best) and candidate < best):\n            best = candidate\n    \n    return best\n```",
