      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maxSumOfSquares(nums, k):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # Count set bits across all numbers for each bit position\n    bit_count = [0] * 32\n    for num in nums:\n        for i in range(32):\n            if num & (1 << i):\n                bit_count[i] += 1\n    \n    # Reconstruct the array optimally: maximize individual numbers\n    new_nums = []\n    # Create as many large numbers as possible by maximizing higher bits first\n    for _ in range(n):\n        num = 0\n        for i in range(31, -1, -1):\n            if bit_count[i] > 0:\n                num |= (1 << i)\n                bit_count[i] -= 1\n        new_nums.append(num)\n    \n    # Take the largest k numbers (already sorted in descending order by construction)\n    result = 0\n    for i in range(k):\n        result = (result + new_nums[i] * new_nums[i]) % MOD\n    \n    return result\n```",
