    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    index = 0\n    t = int(data[index])\n    index += 1\n    results = []\n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(data[index])\n        index += 1\n        k = int(data[index])\n        index += 1\n        a = [int(data[index + i]) for i in range(n)]\n        index += n\n        if k == 2:\n            min_ops = 1\n            for x in a:\n                if x % 2 == 0:\n                    min_ops = 0\n                    break\n            results.append(str(min_ops))\n        elif k == 3:\n            min_ops = 2\n            for x in a:\n                r = x % 3\n                cost = (3 - r) % 3\n                if cost < min_ops:\n                    min_ops = cost\n            results.append(str(min_ops))\n        elif k == 5:\n            min_ops = 4\n            for x in a:\n                r = x % 5\n                cost = (5 - r) % 5\n                if cost < min_ops:\n                    min_ops = cost\n            results.append(str(min_ops))\n        elif k == 4:\n            costs_even = []\n            min_cost4 = 3\n            for x in a:\n                r = x % 4\n                cost4 = (4 - r) % 4\n                if cost4 < min_cost4:\n                    min_cost4 = cost4\n                r2 = x % 2\n                cost2 = (2 - r2) % 2\n                costs_even.append(cost2)\n            costs_even.sort()\n            cost_two_even = costs_even[0] + costs_even[1] if n >= 2 else float('inf')\n            min_ops = min(min_cost4, cost_two_even)\n            results.append(str(min_ops))\n    print('\\n'.join(results))\n\nsolve()\n```",
