    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_119",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given two arrays nums1 and nums2 consisting of positive integers.\nYou have to replace all the 0's in both arrays with strictly positive integers such that the sum of elements of both arrays becomes equal.\nReturn the minimum equal sum you can obtain, or -1 if it is impossible.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums1 = [3,2,0,1,0], nums2 = [6,5,0]\nOutput: 12\nExplanation: We can replace 0's in the following way:\n- Replace the two 0's in nums1 with the values 2 and 4. The resulting array is nums1 = [3,2,2,1,4].\n- Replace the 0 in nums2 with the value 1. The resulting array is nums2 = [6,5,1].\nBoth arrays have an equal sum of 12. It can be shown that it is the minimum sum we can obtain.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums1 = [2,0,2,0], nums2 = [1,4]\nOutput: -1\nExplanation: It is impossible to make the sum of both arrays equal.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= nums1.length, nums2.length <= 10^5\n0 <= nums1[i], nums2[i] <= 10^6",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef min_equal_sum(nums1, nums2):\n    sum1 = sum(nums1)\n    sum2 = sum(nums2)\n    zeros1 = nums1.count(0)\n    zeros2 = nums2.count(0)\n    \n    # If no zeros in either array, check if sums already equal\n    if zeros1 == 0 and zeros2 == 0:\n        return sum1 if sum1 == sum2 else -1\n    \n    # Minimum possible sums (replace zeros with 1)\n    min_sum1 = sum1 + zeros1\n    min_sum2 = sum2 + zeros2\n    \n    # If one side has no zeros but its current sum < other's minimum, impossible\n    if zeros1 == 0 and sum1 < min_sum2:\n        return -1\n    if zeros2 == 0 and sum2 < min_sum1:\n        return -1\n    \n    # Target sum must be >= max(min_sum1, min_sum2)\n    target = max(min_sum1, min_sum2)\n    \n    # Check feasibility: ensure target - sum1 >= zeros1 and target - sum2 >= zeros2\n    if target - sum1 >= zeros1 and target - sum2 >= zeros2:\n        return target\n    return -1\n```",
