      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef theMaximumAchievableX(num: int, t: int) -> int:\n    # Each operation changes both x and num by ±1, so their difference remains constant.\n    # To make x equal to num after operations, we need x - (decreases) = num + (increases)\n    # Since each operation reduces x by 1 and increases num by 1, difference reduces by 2 per operation.\n    # Initial difference = x - num. After t operations: x - num - 2t = 0 → x = num + 2t\n    return num + 2 * t\n```",
