      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumCost(source, target, original, changed, cost):\n    # Initialize 26x26 matrix with infinity for character conversions\n    # dist[i][j] represents minimum cost to convert character i to character j\n    INF = float('inf')\n    dist = [[INF] * 26 for _ in range(26)]\n    \n    # Distance from a character to itself is 0\n    for i in range(26):\n        dist[i][i] = 0\n    \n    # Fill in direct conversion costs\n    for i in range(len(original)):\n        u = ord(original[i]) - ord('a')\n        v = ord(changed[i]) - ord('a')\n        # Take minimum cost if multiple edges between same pair\n        dist[u][v] = min(dist[u][v], cost[i])\n    \n    # Floyd-Warshall algorithm to find shortest paths between all pairs\n    for k in range(26):\n        for i in range(26):\n            if dist[i][k] != INF:  # Optimization: skip if no path to k\n                for j in range(26):\n                    if dist[i][k] + dist[k][j] < dist[i][j]:\n                        dist[i][j] = dist[i][k] + dist[k][j]\n    \n    # Calculate total cost to convert source to target\n    total_cost = 0\n    for i in range(len(source)):\n        s_char = ord(source[i]) - ord('a')\n        t_char = ord(target[i]) - ord('a')\n        \n        if dist[s_char][t_char] == INF:\n            return -1\n        \n        total_cost += dist[s_char][t_char]\n    \n    return total_cost\n```",
