      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef min_operations(nums, target):\n    from collections import Counter\n    \n    cnt = Counter(nums)\n    operations = 0\n    \n    # Process each bit of target\n    for i in range(31):\n        bit = 1 << i\n        \n        if target & bit:\n            # Need this bit in the subsequence\n            if cnt[bit]:\n                cnt[bit] -= 1\n            else:\n                # Find smallest larger power available\n                j = i + 1\n                while j < 31 and not cnt[1 << j]:\n                    j += 1\n                \n                if j == 31:\n                    return -1  # Not possible\n                \n                # Break down nums[j] into i\n                operations += j - i\n                cnt[1 << j] -= 1\n                \n                # Add intermediate powers\n                for k in range(j - 1, i - 1, -1):\n                    cnt[1 << k] += 1\n        \n        # Carry over extra smaller bits to next power\n        if cnt[bit] > 1:\n            cnt[1 << (i + 1)] += cnt[bit] // 2\n            cnt[bit] = cnt[bit] % 2\n    \n    return operations\n```",
