    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef getSmallestString(s: str, k: int) -> str:\n    n = len(s)\n    res = list(s)\n    \n    # Try to make each character as small as possible (greedy approach)\n    # For each position, try changing it to 'a', then 'b', etc., until we can't anymore\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        original_char = ord(res[i]) - ord('a')\n        \n        # Try changing to each character from 'a' to 'z'\n        for target in range(26):  # target from 0 ('a') to 25 ('z')\n            # Calculate cyclic distance between original char and target char\n            dist = min(abs(original_char - target), 26 - abs(original_char - target))\n            \n            if dist <= k:\n                res[i] = chr(target + ord('a'))\n                k -= dist\n                break\n    \n    return ''.join(res)\n```",
