    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minOperations(s: str) -> int:\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    # The key insight: \n    # We want all characters to be the same, either all '0' or all '1'.\n    # Consider making all characters equal to s[0]. \n    # Traverse the string from left to right. \n    # Every time s[i] != s[i-1], we need to flip either the prefix [0..i-1] or suffix [i..n-1].\n    # For position i where s[i] != s[i-1]:\n    #   - Flipping prefix [0..i-1] costs i\n    #   - Flipping suffix [i..n-1] costs n-i\n    # We choose the cheaper option for each transition.\n    \n    total_cost = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if s[i] != s[i-1]:\n            total_cost += min(i, n - i)\n    \n    return total_cost\n```",
