      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimum_operations(num: str) -> int:\n    n = len(num)\n    \n    # Find the rightmost '0' or '5' as the last digit of potential special number\n    # For a number to be divisible by 25, it must end with 00, 25, 50, or 75\n    \n    min_ops = n  # worst case: delete all digits\n    \n    # Check for all possible endings: \"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"\n    endings = [\"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"]\n    \n    for end in endings:\n        # Find the second character of the ending first (from right to left)\n        j = end[1]\n        pos2 = -1\n        for i in range(n-1, -1, -1):\n            if num[i] == j:\n                pos2 = i\n                break\n        \n        if pos2 == -1:\n            continue\n        \n        # Find the first character of the ending before pos2\n        k = end[0]\n        pos1 = -1\n        for i in range(pos2-1, -1, -1):\n            if num[i] == k:\n                pos1 = i\n                break\n        \n        if pos1 == -1:\n            continue\n        \n        # Operations needed = delete all digits except those at pos1 and pos2\n        ops = (n - pos2 - 1) + (pos2 - pos1 - 1)\n        min_ops = min(min_ops, ops)\n    \n    # Special case: if we have a '0' anywhere, we can make \"0\" which is divisible by 25\n    # This requires deleting all other digits\n    if '0' in num:\n        # Count operations to keep just one '0'\n        first_zero_pos = num.index('0')\n        ops = n - 1  # delete all except one digit, which is '0'\n        min_ops = min(min_ops, ops)\n    \n    return min_ops\n```",
