    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_53",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given a binary array nums.\nA subarray of an array is good if it contains exactly one element with the value 1.\nReturn an integer denoting the number of ways to split the array nums into good subarrays. As the number may be too large, return it modulo 10^9 + 7.\nA subarray is a contiguous non-empty sequence of elements within an array.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [0,1,0,0,1]\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: There are 3 ways to split nums into good subarrays:\n- [0,1] [0,0,1]\n- [0,1,0] [0,1]\n- [0,1,0,0] [1]\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [0,1,0]\nOutput: 1\nExplanation: There is 1 way to split nums into good subarrays:\n- [0,1,0]\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= nums.length <= 10^5\n0 <= nums[i] <= 1",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef numberOfGoodSubarraySplits(nums):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    \n    # Find positions of all 1s\n    ones_positions = [i for i, val in enumerate(nums) if val == 1]\n    \n    # If there are no 1s, no good subarrays possible\n    if not ones_positions:\n        return 0\n    \n    # If there's only one 1, there's exactly one way to split\n    if len(ones_positions) == 1:\n        return 1\n    \n    # For multiple 1s, the number of ways is the product of distances between consecutive 1s\n    # between each pair of consecutive 1s, we can place the split point in (position[i+1] - position[i]) ways\n    result = 1\n    for i in range(1, len(ones_positions)):\n        # Number of ways to split between ones_positions[i-1] and ones_positions[i]\n        # is the distance between them (since we can split anywhere in between, including right after the first 1)\n        ways = ones_positions[i] - ones_positions[i-1]\n        result = (result * ways) % MOD\n    \n    return result\n```",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
