      "generated_answer": "In his critique of the \"numbers argument,\" Derek Parfit notes that both Taurek and Lewis assume that for an aggregate sum of pain to be mathematically or morally additive, it must be experienced by a single individual. This assumption is crucial to their arguments regarding why the number of people suffering does not necessarily provide a reason to prioritize them over an individual. Therefore, they insist that only the internal aggregation within one person's life permits the notion of a \"sum of pain.\"\n\n\\boxed{E}",
