    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the degree of skewness (Pearson's coefficient), we calculate the mean ($\\bar{x} \\approx 65.2$), the median ($\\tilde{x} \\approx 66.25$), and the standard deviation ($s \\approx 7.15$). Using the formula $Skewness = 3(\\bar{x} - \\tilde{x}) / s$, we get $3(65.2 - 66.25) / 7.15 \\approx -0.44$. This value corresponds to the calculated skewness of the distribution.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
