      "generated_answer": "The Dickey-Fuller distribution is skewed to the left and has a distribution that is more dispersed than the standard normal distribution. Because the unit root test rejects the null hypothesis at the left tail, the critical values of the Dickey-Fuller distribution are located further to the left (more negative) than those of the standard normal distribution. Therefore, for a given significance level, the Dickey-Fuller statistic must be more negative than the corresponding normal distribution value to reject the null hypothesis.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
