    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine if the process $y_t = 1.5y_{t-1} - 0.5y_{t-2} + u_t$ is stationary, we examine the characteristic equation $1 - 1.5z + 0.5z^2 = 0$. Factoring this yields $(1 - z)(1 - 0.5z) = 0$, revealing roots at $z_1 = 1$ and $z_2 = 2$. Since one root lies on the unit circle and the other lies outside it, the process contains a unit root and is therefore non-stationary.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
