      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nEconomic gains alone do not define exploitation, as trade theory suggests that voluntary exchange typically generates mutual benefits regardless of the absolute difference in wealth. Determining exploitation would require analyzing factors such as labor conditions, power imbalances, and the long-term impact on domestic development rather than just trade outcomes. Therefore, the simple monetary difference does not provide enough information to conclude whether exploitation is occurring.",
