    "for_optimality": false
  },
  {
    "global index": "AIME_7",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the three-digit positive integer $\\underline{{a}}\\,\\underline{{b}}\\,\\underline{{c}}$ whose representation in base nine is $\\underline{{b}}\\,\\underline{{c}}\\,\\underline{{a}}_{{\\,\\text{{nine}},$ where $a,$ $b,$ and $c$ are (not necessarily distinct) digits.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The three-digit base-10 number \\(\\underline{a b c}\\) equals \\(100a + 10b + c\\). Its base-9 representation \\(\\underline{b c a}_9\\) equals \\(81b + 9c + a\\). Equating the two expressions yields the Diophantine equation\n\\[\n99a = 71b + 8c.\n\\]\nThe admissible ranges are \\(a,b\\in\\{1,\\dots,8\\}\\) and \\(c\\in\\{0,\\dots,8\\}\\). Reducing the equation modulo 8 produces the linear congruence\n\\[\na\\equiv 5b\\pmod{8}.\n\\]\nTesting each admissible \\(b\\) shows that the only triple satisfying both the congruence and the range constraints on \\(c\\) is\n\\[\na=2,\\quad b=2,\\quad c=7.\n\\]\nDirect substitution confirms\n\\[\n100\\cdot2+10\\cdot2+7=227=2\\cdot81+7\\cdot9+2.\n\\]\nThus the unique solution is the integer 227.\n\n\\boxed{227}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 261,
        "output_tokens": 1292,
        "total_tokens": 1553
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3",
