    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "A lattice path from \\((0,0)\\) to \\((8,8)\\) using only right and up unit steps consists of alternating horizontal and vertical runs whose lengths are positive integers. Exactly four direction changes therefore requires precisely five runs whose lengths sum to 8 in each coordinate direction.\n\nThere are two admissible patterns:\n- H-V-H-V-H (three horizontal runs summing to 8, two vertical runs summing to 8). The number of positive integer solutions is \\(\\binom{7}{2}=21\\) for the horizontal runs and \\(\\binom{7}{1}=7\\) for the vertical runs, giving \\(21\\times7=147\\) paths.\n- V-H-V-H-V yields the symmetric count \\(147\\).\n\nAdding both cases produces the total\n\\[\n2\\times\\binom{7}{2}\\binom{7}{1}=294.\n\\]\nBecause every step is right or up, every such sequence stays inside the \\(8\\times8\\) grid.\n\n\\boxed{294}",
