    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the present ages be: father \\(F\\), elder son \\(E\\), younger son \\(Y\\). Given \\(E = Y + 2\\) and \\(E + Y = F - 14\\) so \\(2Y + 2 = F - 14\\) → \\(F = 2Y + 16\\). Ten years ago, \\((E-10)+(Y-10) = \\frac{1}{3}(F-10)\\) → \\(E+Y-20 = \\frac{1}{3}(F-10)\\). Substitute \\(E+Y = 2Y+2\\): \\(2Y+2-20 = \\frac{1}{3}(F-10)\\) → \\(2Y-18 = \\frac{1}{3}(F-10)\\) → multiply by 3: \\(6Y-54 = F-10\\) → \\(F = 6Y-44\\). Equate: \\(2Y+16 = 6Y-44\\) → \\(60 = 4Y\\) → \\(Y=15\\), then \\(E=17\\), \\(F=46\\). Thus present ages: father 46, elder son 17, younger son 15.\n\n\\boxed{46, 17, 15}",
