    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements best explains the bid-rent theory?\n\nOptions: \nA. Land value is highest in the central business district, and land value decreases with distance from the CBD.\nB. Land value is highest in the suburbs, resulting in larger houses.\nC. More space is available in the urban core because most growth is upward.\nD. Land value is higher in the suburbs due to a greater demand for land there.\nE. Land value is constant throughout the metropolitan area due to the high demand for residential space in general.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The bid-rent theory states that land values are highest at the center of a city (the central business district) due to competition for access to commercial activity, and they decrease as distance from the CBD increases. This pattern reflects the willingness of businesses and individuals to pay more for central locations, with residential users valuing peripheral areas more. Thus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}",
