    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the total probability, we count the successful outcomes for a pair of dice: there are 4 ways to roll a 5 (1,4; 4,1; 2,3; 3,2), 5 ways to roll a 6 (1,5; 5,1; 2,4; 4,2; 3,3), and 6 ways to roll a 7 (1,6; 6,1; 2,5; 5,2; 3,4; 4,3). Summing these gives $4 + 5 + 6 = 15$ successful outcomes out of 36 total possibilities. Dividing 15/36 by 3/3 simplifies to 5/12.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
