    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the fundamental period of the given function:\n$$f(x)=\\left\\{{\\begin{{array}}{{ll}}(-1)^n, & 2 n-1 \\leq x<2 n, \\\\ 1, & 2 n \\leq x<2 n+1 ;\\end{{array}} \\quad n=0, \\pm 1, \\pm 2, \\ldots\\right.$$\n\nOptions: \nA. √2 (the square root of 2)\nB. 2\nC. 5\nD. 3\nE. π (pi)\nF. 1\nG. 6\nH. 2.5\nI. 8\nJ.  4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the fundamental period, we examine the values of $f(x)$ across intervals of length 2: $f(x) = (-1)^n$ for $x \\in [2n-1, 2n)$ and $f(x) = 1$ for $x \\in [2n, 2n+1)$. Evaluating consecutive intervals, we see $f(x)$ takes values of $-1, 1, 1, 1, -1, 1, 1, 1, \\dots$ which implies a pattern repeating every 4 units. Thus, the fundamental period is 4.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
