      "generated_answer": "The power of a lens ($P$) in diopters is the reciprocal of the focal length ($f$) in meters, so $f = 1 / -5 = -0.2$ meters, or $-20$ cm. Because $P$ is negative, the lens is concave (diverging), which always produces an upright, virtual image of a distant object (at infinity) located at the focal point in front of the lens. Thus, the image is virtual, upright, and located 20 cm in front of the eyes.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
