    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The expression $2^n$ is a power of 2, which for any integer $n \\geq 1$ results in a number that is only prime if the result is 2 itself (when $n=1$). Since $2^1 = 2$ (prime) and $2^2 = 4$, the smallest value of $n$ for which $2^n$ is not a prime number is $n=2$. Comparing this to the given options, the value corresponds to option A (and G).\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
