    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the price of shoes be \\( s \\) and boots be \\( b \\).  \nFrom Monday: \\( 22s + 16b = 540 \\).  \nFrom Tuesday: \\( 8s + 32b = 720 \\).  \nMultiply the Monday equation by 2: \\( 44s + 32b = 1080 \\). Subtract the Tuesday equation: \\((44s + 32b) - (8s + 32b) = 1080 - 720\\), so \\( 36s = 360\\), giving \\( s = 10 \\).  \nSubstitute back: \\( 22(10) + 16b = 540 \\Rightarrow 220 + 16b = 540 \\Rightarrow 16b = 320 \\Rightarrow b = 20 \\).  \nThus boots cost \\( 20 - 10 = 10 \\) dollars more.  \n\n\\boxed{C}",
