      "generated_answer": "We need to compute two probabilities:  \n\n(a) Probability of no ace and no king:  \nThere are 8 such cards (4 aces + 4 kings) removed from 52, so choose 13 from the remaining 44.  \n\\[\nP = \\frac{\\binom{44}{13}}{\\binom{52}{13}} \\approx 0.0818\n\\]  \n\n(b) Probability of (no ace or exactly one ace) and exactly four kings:  \nFor no ace and 4 kings, you need 4 of 4 kings and 9 from the 44 non-ace, non-king cards. For 1 ace and 4 kings, you pick 1 ace from 4, 4 kings from 4, and 8 from 44 non-ace, non-king. Sum both combinations and divide by \\(\\binom{52}{13}\\), giving \\(\\approx 0.0022\\).  \n\nThe match is **0.0818, 0.0022**, which corresponds to option G.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{G}\n\\]",
