    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the eigenvalues, we calculate the roots of the characteristic equation $\\det(A - \\lambda I) = 0$ for each matrix:\n(a) For $\\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\end{pmatrix}$, $(3-\\lambda)^2 - 1 = 0 \\Rightarrow (3-\\lambda) = \\pm 1$, yielding $\\lambda = 4, 2$.\n(b) For $\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\end{pmatrix}$, the characteristic equation is $(1-\\lambda)^2(5-\\lambda) = 0$, yielding $\\lambda = 1, 1, 5$.\n(c) For $\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 4 & 6 \\\\ -8 & 0 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}$, the characteristic equation is $(-\\lambda^3 + 3\\lambda^2 + \\lambda - 3) = 0$, which factors to $-( \\lambda-3)(\\lambda-1)(\\lambda+1) = 0$, yielding $\\lambda = 3, 1, -1$. \n\nThese results correspond to option I.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
