      "generated_answer": "The initial value of \\( f(t) = e^{-2t} u(t) \\) at \\( t = 0^+ \\) is 1, and the slope (derivative) at \\( t = 0^+ \\) is \\(-2\\). The initial-value theorem confirms the initial value as \\(\\lim_{s \\to \\infty} s F(s) = 1\\), but the theorem for the derivative does not apply due to the presence of an impulse in \\( f'(t) \\). Thus, the correct choice is J.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
