    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The average heat transfer coefficient is derived from equating total heat transfer: \\(Q = \\int h_x (T_s - T) dA = h_{av} A (T_s - T)_{av}\\). For a pipe, \\(dA = 2\\pi R dx\\) and \\(A = 2\\pi R L\\), leading to \\(h_{av} = \\frac{\\int_0^L h_x (T_s - T) dx}{L (T_s - T)_{av}}\\). Using the given definition \\((T_s - T)_{av} = T_s - T_{av}\\), this simplifies to option B, which correctly expresses the integral over the temperature difference and the average temperature difference.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
