      "generated_answer": "To calculate the relative risk, divide the risk of outcome in the exposed group by the risk of outcome in the unexposed group. The risk for the exposed group (Drug X) is 100/200 = 0.5, and the risk for the unexposed group is 100/400 = 0.25. Dividing 0.5 by 0.25 results in a relative risk of 2.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
